```

---

# 🔥 STEP 1.7 — Freeing memory (Postorder)

```c
void free_tree(struct Node* root) {
    if (root == NULL) return;
    free_tree(root->left);    // free left subtree
    free_tree(root->right);   // free right subtree
    free(root);               // finally free current node
}
```

👉 **Why postorder?**  
Because if you free the parent first, you lose access to its children → memory leak.  
By freeing children first, nothing is lost.  

